    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28413" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕgăreus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ),
		i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μεγαρεύς</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a son of Neptune, and father of Hippomenes</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 157</span></i> and 185; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 10,
				605</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕgărēĭus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to Megareus, Megareian</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">heros,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Hippomenes</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 659</span></i>
			.</div>
